  "reasoning": "The facts describe two distinct illegal behaviors by the public official Qu. The first set of acts involves using his position as village head to collect land purchase payments and agricultural compensation and keep part of the money for himself, which matches the statutory offense of 职务侵占 (occupation of public funds by a person in a position of authority). The second set of acts involves abusing his role in managing state grain subsidies, low‑income subsidies, rural housing assistance, and land‑transfer project funds, employing false reports, misappropriation, and embezzlement of public money, which corresponds to the crime of 贪污 (embezzlement by a public official). Both offenses are distinct and should be charged together.\nTherefore, the appropriate charges are 职务侵占 and 贪污.",
